# Server TEST environment — EXAMPLE ONLY. Fake values; never a real secret (rules S1, S2).
#
# The server suite runs against THROWAWAY test databases and a SEPARATE Redis keyspace.
# Create the test databases once (idempotent):
#     node scripts/db-create-test-databases.mjs
#
# Mode A (this file): copy it to server/.env.test (git-ignored) and fill the three names below
# with your local values (ports/passwords from your .env — keep them in .env, never here).
# Mode B (default, nothing set): the suite derives <database name>_test and Redis index 15 from
# the dev URLs in .env. No file needed for the normal local setup.
#
# Guard rules (enforced before any test runs, message names variables only, never values):
#   - host must be local (localhost / 127.0.0.1 / ::1);
#   - database names must end in `_test` and must not equal the dev database names;
#   - TEST_REDIS_URL must select a keyspace other than the dev one (index 15 by convention).
# The suite REFUSES to run against the dev databases or the dev Redis keyspace.
TEST_DB0_WRITE_URL=postgresql://rowta:CHANGE_ME_FAKE@localhost:5442/rowta_db0_test
TEST_DB1_WRITE_URL=postgresql://rowta:CHANGE_ME_FAKE@localhost:5443/rowta_db1_test
TEST_REDIS_URL=redis://:CHANGE_ME_FAKE@localhost:6390/15
